Abstract = {Crowd estimation is considered as an attractive technique for indoor
   energy saving, route guidance, etc. Generally, crowd estimation consists
   of crowd density estimation and crowd counting. In vision-based approach
   of crowd estimation, there are several researches addressing both crowd
   counting and localization. However, most of sensor or radio-based
   approaches are focusing on crowd counting only. In this study, we assess
   the potential of simultaneous crowd counting and localization by using
   WiFi CSI and machine learning.},
