   Systems-WFCS-Annual, University of Rostock, Rostock, GERMANY, JUN 10-13,
   2025},
Organization = {Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc; IEEE Industrial
   Electronics Society},
Abstract = {The fields of human presence detection (HPD) and people counting (PC)
   from WiFi-Channel State Information (CSI) represent constantly evolving
   areas of research within the scientific community. This study aims to
   expand the research frontiers by exploring the application of HPD and PC
   in an industrial environment characterized by its considerable
   dimensions, the presence of obstacles and machines, and harsh
   propagation channel conditions. Using a convolutional neural network
   (CNN) incorporating CSI measurements, we demonstrated the ability to
   distinguish between human presence and industrial machine activity with
   the same model, achieving an accuracy of over 99\%. In addition, a study
   was conducted to count up to three people, even when machines were on,
   with an accuracy of over 92\%. Another experiment was conducted with the
   objective of assessing not only the feasibility of PC in a naturally
   challenging environment but also the impact of the WiFi channel
   bandwidth in this particular application. The results of this study
   highlight the potential of WiFi-CSI sensing to address a significant
   challenge in human activity detection and estimation: its application in
   industrial environments.},
