   Lockheed Martin; Trexon; OPHIR RF; Interface Concept; Assoc Old Crows;
   Capella Space; Empower RF Syst Inc; Mathworks; Adv Protect Syst; Opt
   Zonu; RFHIC US; METRON},
Abstract = {In this paper, we consider the problem of crowd counting using
   millimeter-wave radars. In contrast to conventional detect-and-track
   counting schemes, the method operates on a power metric derived from the
   range-Doppler maps. The system is evaluated at the VIP area in the
   Tomorrowland 2022 music festival. The analysis is carried out over crowd
   sizes of 0 to 1500 people, where we measure a 82.9\% to 94.2\%
   correlation with the bracelet crowd counting reference obtained from the
   access control system. The results suggest relative counting errors
   within +/- 50\% for small crowds and within +/- 25\% for large crowds as
   measured by the 95\% percentile prediction intervals.},
