Series = {International Symposium on Advanced Topics in Electrical Engineering},
Year = {2021},
Note = {12th International Symposium on Advanced Topics in Electrical
   Engineering (ATEE), Bucharest, ROMANIA, MAR 25-27, 2021},
Abstract = {The current pandemic caused by the SARS-CoV-2 virus has affected all
   sectors of activity through quarantine measures imposed to stop the
   spread of the disease. In the absence of safe treatment, social
   distancing and wearing a face mask are the only weapons to combat this
   pandemic. Unfortunately, social distance has led to the migration of
   education to a distance format reducing the interaction between teachers
   and students. Even if, through the vaccination process, the spread of
   COVID-19 disease will be slowed down, the physical return to schools and
   universities will be done under the sign of social distancing and health
   precautions. This article proposes a simple and low-cost solution for
   monitoring the density of people in a room by monitoring WiFi traffic.
   Because the solution can be implemented on a large scale, it is suitable
   for implementation as a centralized monitoring and warning solution at
   school or university campus level.},
